Implementing a multi-treelist (also known as a tree grid or hierarchical list) within an Angular application involves several steps, including setting up the environment, creating the data structure for your treemaps, and rendering them using Angular components.

### Step 1: Set Up Your Angular Project

First, ensure you have Node.js installed on your machine. Then, create a new Angular project:

```bash
ng new my-multitreelist-app
cd my-multitreelist-app
```

### Step 2: Install Required Packages

For this example, we'll use `@angular/material` for UI components like `MatTreeGrid`, which is not officially part of core Angular but can be used via npm packages.

Install the necessary packages:

```bash
npm install @swimlane/ngx-treegrid @swimlane/ngx-charts mat-datetime-pickers mat-calendar mat-tdp-datepicker --save
```

### Step 3: Create Data Structure

Assume you want to display data similar to how it would look in a typical treemap visualization. For simplicity, let's say we're displaying categories and their subcategories.

```typescript
// src/app/data.ts
export interface Category {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  children?: Category[];
}

const rootCategories: Category[] = [
  {
    id: 'category1',
    name: 'Category 1'
  },
  {
    id: 'category2',
    name: 'Category 2',
    children: [
      {
        id: 'subcategory1a',
        name: 'Subcategory 1A'
      },
      {
        id: 'subcategory1b',
        name: 'Subcategory 1B'
      }
    ]
  },
  // Add more categories here...
];
```

### Step 4: Create TreeGrid Component

Create a component that will render the treegrid:

```typescript
// src/app/tree-grid.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { MatTreeGridComponent } from '@swimlane/ngx-treegrid';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-tree-grid',
  template: `
    <mat-tree-grid #treeGrid>
      <mat-tree-node *ngFor="let category of categories" [item]="category">
        {{ category.name }}
        <mat-tree-node *ngIf="category.children?.length > 0" [ref]="childNodeRef"></mat-tree-node>
      </mat-tree-node>
    </mat-tree-grid>
  `,
})
export class TreeGridComponent implements OnInit {
  categories: Category[];

  constructor(private treeGrid: MatTreeGridComponent<{}, Category>) {}

  ngOnInit(): void {
    this.treeGrid.categories = rootCategories;
  }

  get childNodeRef() {
    return this.treeGrid.ref.find((node): node is MatTreeNode => !!node);
  }
}
```

### Step 5: Update App Module

In your app module, import and configure the treegrid component:

```typescript
// src/app/app.module.ts
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { AppComponent } from './app.component';
import { TreeGridComponent } from './tree-grid.component';
import { MatTreeGridModule } from '@swimlane/ngx-treegrid';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    AppComponent,
    TreeGridComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule,
    MatTreeGridModule
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

### Step 6: Run the Application

Now run your Angular application:

```bash
ng serve
```

Open your browser and navigate to `http://localhost:4200`.

